From: Codex local A376B compatibility adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt reviewed AZH4 optical fingerprint flags to rear capacitive

Reason: product-tail-after-hdr.txt aborts at optical -> rear fingerprint SPF handling. AZH4 retains Samsung REAR=3 and CAPACITANCE=1 enums, the HIDL mapper maps Samsung REAR to Android TYPE_REAR=1, and BiometricSetting retains a rear feature path. Set the reviewed framework sensor position/type and disable optical/in-display constants in services/SystemUI and the pinned compatibility BiometricSetting SIDE constant. Preserve the target native HAL/blob and all unrelated initializer registers.
Files: unica/patches/product_feature/customize.sh; unica/patches/product_feature/fingerprint/a376b_rear.py.
Verification: fail-closed exact class/method/body checks before writing; actual donor Smali preflight and assembly through fork apktool; patch replay byte comparison. Enrollment, unlock and gesture behavior require runtime logs. No kernel or device writes.


Provenance: device-stack star2lte overlay BiometricSetting APK SHA256 bc64ca2e5083ae651a57e523eb68496ccf6f9dcaeabfed32c3adc1998acb877c; its DisplayStateManager uses Context constructors and no donor product string, checked explicitly. Feature-driven rear/display/optical paths retained.

